pital of 8.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.30).","It converts 8% of revenue into free cash flow.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 8%.","ROE of 0% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.6x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 10pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.8x net debt to EBITDA ($109.2M of cash against $918.1M of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.5x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.66 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.7% over 3 years and 29.1% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 52%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Margins are contracting (-2.5% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 25%.","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (10.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 36, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.6%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 8.3% a year to shareholders (4.5% in buybacks and 2.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 4.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 37 employees, each generates about $25.9M of revenue, 11.4x the Real Estate median, and revenue has fallen 2.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $2.1M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $235K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":17.3,"head":"Red flag: operating incom